#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:383
msgid "Why is my compliance score so much lower than my accessibility score?"
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:388
#, python-format
msgid ""
"The compliance score requires perfect passes (zero violations) for each "
"test, while the accessibility score gives credit for partial passes. Even"
" if 90%% of your checks pass, a single violation makes that test non-"
"compliant."
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:396
msgid "What WCAG level should I aim for?"
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:401
msgid ""
"Level AA is the recommended target and legal requirement in many "
"jurisdictions. Level A is the absolute minimum, while Level AAA is "
"typically only required for specific content or specialized applications."
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:409
msgid "How often should I run accessibility tests?"
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:414
msgid ""
"Test after every significant change to your site. Set up automated "
"testing in your CI/CD pipeline to catch issues early. Run comprehensive "
"tests at least monthly for active sites."
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:422
msgid "What's the difference between automated and manual testing?"
msgstr ""

#: auto_a11y/web/templates/help.html:427
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Automated testing (like Auto A11y) can catch about 30-40%% of "
"accessibility issues quickly and consistently. Manual testing is needed "
"for subjective criteria like whether alt text is meaningful or if the "
"reading order makes sense. Use both for comprehensive coverage."
msgstr ""

